C["B2_COMPARE_VR-010_WASHING_PLACE_V002_vs_V004.jpg"] = "WASHING PLACE, ANCESTRAL REALM, V002 base to V004 candidate, answering REJECTION_REPORT_VR-010_WASHING_PLACE_V003. Masked removal of the exposed runoff channel only; every named V002 element is its own pixels. Top panels: BASE V002 (unchanged source) and CANDIDATE V004, review required. Crops show the runoff channel before and after, and the slab, pots, dipper and splash earth. Defects listed: 1 (stone washing slab, 0 changed pixels); 2 and 3 (no recess, niche or cavity added at a wall base, 0 changed pixels); 4 (water trough, pot and dipper untouched); 5 (palm-mat screens and posts unaltered, 0 changed pixels); 6 (bright exposed runoff line gone, ground now plain damp earth with no ditch, trench, groove or rut and no water channel drawn); 7 (chrome corrected: header now reads ENV_HOME_SETTLEMENT_WASHING_PLACE_V004, status REVIEW REQUIRED, and the CORRECTED SINCE V002 and KNOWN ISSUES blocks rewritten). Pixel proof vs V002: 113,314 px changed in total, of which 46,197 px are inside the repaint corridor, and 0 are outside the corridor and metadata column. Declared deviation: no wall-base pass-through is drawn, so the drain reads as a flush damp grade that seeps under the screen's shadow, and the outlet itself is off-frame. Status: candidate only, review required, not approved, not canon, not filed; V002 and V001 preserved untouched and the rejected V003 left as rejected."
C["B2_RETOUCH_GUIDE_VR-006_BLOCKED.jpg"] = "Composition sheet headed COMPOSITION, ADANNA IN THE MOTHERS' COURTYARD, COMP_ADANNA_MOTHERS_COURTYARD_V003, status REVIEW REQUIRED, chapter 8, exploratory. A rendered scene shows a woman with a sheathed blade beside a tree, a loom, jars, a broom and a mortar in a mud courtyard. Retouch guide, one object only: point A at her left hip (1560,622) is marked KEEP; point B at the current tip (1760,782) is marked as the fault, with a target line for the tip at or above (1600,880) and the sheath to hang vertically from A. Action: rotate the sheath upright about the hilt, shorten it to about 65 percent of B, rebuild the skirt behind the old diagonal, and keep the mortar and pestle untouched and in front. Must not change: face, hair, costume, ornaments, sandals, stance, hand on pestle, loom cloth, jars, tree, broom and light. Side text: LOCATION CH08-SUB-005, ASSESSMENT REQUIRES REVISION, supersedes V002, which is kept; SCABBARD CHECK shorter than V002 but still too long, placement at her left hip angled back behind the mortar; WHAT WORKS left-side features and courtyard as before, with the approved doorway view set back in by hand; and a correction note to shorten the scabbard by hand on this image. Filename contains BLOCKED; the picture is accessible and fully readable."
C["B2_RETOUCH_GUIDE_VR-007_BLOCKED.jpg"] = "Composition sheet headed COMPOSITION, ADANNA INSIDE NNEKA'S HOUSE, COMP_ADANNA_NNEKAS_HOUSE_INTERIOR_V002, status REVIEW REQUIRED, chapter 8, exploratory. A seated woman on a sleeping platform by an open doorway holds a sheathed weapon, with a folded striped cloth, mat, jars, basket and hearth nearby. Retouch guide, one object only: point A at the spiral pommel (1545,690) is marked KEEP; point B at the chape disc (1357,940) is marked MOVE UP. The target line for the tip is no lower than y 865, and the current lowest point is y 940. The sheath is currently 383 px long, about 90 to 100 cm. Action: shorten along the axis about A to about 70 percent so the tip lands on the green line, re-seat the chape disc at the new tip, and rebuild the skirt and platform shadow behind the removed section. Must not change: face, hair, costume, hands, cloth, hearth, doorway view, mat, jars, basket and light. Notes: no bare blade, no second weapon, nothing on the sleeping platform. Side text: LOCATION CH08-INT-001, approved environment NNEKAS_HOUSE_INTERIOR_V003, scene CH08-SCN-001; ASSESSMENT submitted for review with one fault noted, supersedes V001, which is kept; READ seated on the sleeping platform, turned toward the door; FIXED SINCE V001 the hearth is three stones with a pot again; RECURRING FAULT the scabbard is drawn longer than the approved short blade (about 60 cm); STORY NOTE the folded cloth is a staging idea only and establishes nothing. Filename contains BLOCKED; the picture is accessible and fully readable."
C["ENV_CH03-INT-004_THE_FORGOTTEN_KITCHEN_V002.jpg"] = "Desaturated grey view of a stone-walled kitchen with fine grey particles in the air. A clay cooking pot sits on three stones over grey ash, herb bundles hang from a pole across the upper wall, and a dark doorway opening is at the back. Stacked round grinding stones with a shallow stone bowl sit at right, with a long pole leaning at the far right. An open doorway at left shows bare trees and pale ground outside."
C["B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V005_vs_V007.jpg"] = "Base and candidate panels, ESTABLISHING VIEW ANCESTRAL REALM, V005 base to V007 candidate, answering REJECTION_REPORT_ESTABLISHING_V006. Masked architectural repaint of the settlement mound only; everything outside the mask is V005's own pixels. The base V005 shows a regular stepped cone of houses at right. The candidate V007 replaces the cone with an irregular heap of separate single-storey mud-and-thatch houses with ladders and worn stair runs. Lower crops show the mound and the mound foot where it meets the foreground. Sheet text: defect A (the regular symmetrical cone is gone), defect B (the wall smear was a V006-only artefact, zero hand-retouch smears, zero figures), defect C (board and register claims not repeated), defect E (chrome: header V005 to V007, CLIENT REVIEW and CHANGED SINCE V005 and KNOWN ISSUES rewritten, status REVIEW REQUIRED, EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON and consultant-review disclaimer retained). Pixel proof: 441,432 px total changed versus V005, 365,251 px inside the mask, 0 outside mask plus chrome; Hall of Posts, aerial river and foreground compound are V005 pixels untouched. OPEN: Nneka's warm-daylight house is not yet placed and is declared in KNOWN ISSUES. Status: candidate only, review required, not approved, not canon, not filed; V005 and rejected V006 are preserved untouched."
C["B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING.jpg"] = "Side-by-side comparison headed ESTABLISHING VIEW ENV_LAST_DAUGHTER_ANCESTRAL_REALM_ESTABLISHING, V005 master to V006 candidate, both REVIEW REQUIRED. The left panel is the V005 master: mud houses with thatched roofs, a long open-sided hall on pillars at left, and a stepped cone of houses at right under a hazy warm sky. The right panel is the V006 candidate: the mound is rebuilt as an irregular stack of individual houses with stepped shoulders, ladders and stair runs, one low house lit by warm low sun, and the outline is close to the master at this size. Sheet text: no V006 exists in the drive, so V005 is the source and V006 is the output. Defects addressed: the mound is still too regular a cone, and one house in warm daylight (Nneka's) is not visible. Additional change declared: the generative pass placed a small standing figure in a yard, and this was removed by hand (figureless by client decision, OAD-40). Residual: the overhead reflection of the settlement is more abstract than V005, colours are warmer, and the foreground compound layout differs. Change outside the panel: none (diff 0)."
C["B2_COMPARE_WALL_OF_HOUSES.jpg"] = "WALL OF HOUSES, ENV_LAST_DAUGHTER_ANCESTRAL_REALM_WALL_OF_HOUSES, V003 master to V004 candidate, both REVIEW REQUIRED. Both panels show a foggy mound of mud-brick houses with thatched roofs stacked up a slope. Sheet text: no V004 exists in the drive, so V003 is the source and V004 is the output. Defects addressed: several houses are two-storey blocks, the first settlement at the foot is not distinct, and sealed doorways do not read at this distance. Resolution: every building is single-storey with one roof and one opening, the foot of the mound carries separate freestanding houses with gaps and paths, and the sealed doorways are pale plastered panels with visible cracks, one clearly fractured. The V004 candidate shows bluer, paler fog, the freestanding houses with doorways at the foot, and two pale plastered doorway panels. Residual, as printed on the sheet: fog is heavier at the top than V003, the palette is redder, and the mound silhouette is broader. Change outside the panel: none (diff 0)."
